        "noise 1.0": {
          "subspace error": 0.3078,
          "naive Frobenius": 1.16
        }
      },
      "error": 0.28561025683016017,
      "status": "PARTIALLY IDENTIFIABLE",
      "control": "the same quantity scored in Frobenius norm, which stays near 1 at every noise level",
      "notes": "the tangent *subspace* is recovered (sin theta = 0.286) while the matrix itself is not (Frobenius 1.30). Blind inversion of A->B has direct error 1.21, dropping to 0.019 once an affine reparameterisation of the latent is allowed. That gap IS Hypothesis 2: what is recoverable is the equivalence class, not the coordinates.",
      "error_label": "sin of the largest principal angle at noise 0.1"
    }
